---
description: Use Flatpack components for Recording Studio UI
globs: "**/*.{erb,html,css,js}"
alwaysApply: false
---

Flatpack is the Rails ViewComponent library. Recording Studio uses it exclusively.

Search https://flatpack.bowerbird.io/ and this repo before you write custom CSS or markup. Compose existing components. Do not rebuild buttons, forms, alerts, cards, modals, or nav.

Semantic layout markup is fine when Flatpack has no structure for that part of the page.

If you need a piece Flatpack does not have, ask whether to add it to Flatpack or (rarely) build custom. Do not invent custom UI in silence.

Do not rewrite unrelated legacy UI just because you opened the file. When you touch a legacy element, migrate that element if the change is local and safe.

Use the core default layout. One primary action per page.

Page shape: `recording-studio-ui`. Copy: `recording-studio-text`. Which component: `recording-studio-flatpack`. Do not restate those skills here.
